<title>MEXICO: BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY OPERATIONS.</title>
<headline>BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY OPERATIONS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and five repurchase agreements it had offered in order to drain 2.498 billion pesos from the secondary market on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    357 days   20.49 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   20.41 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     91 days   19.10 pct</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     54 days   20.50 pct</p>
<p>    700 million     46 days   20.02 pct</p>
<p>    300 million     43 days   19.47 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     14 days   19.47 pct</p>
<p>    148 million	1 day    19.86 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
